<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    android:allowBackup="false" stops CLOUD backup, and from Android 12 (API 31)
    that is no longer the whole story: device-to-device transfer copies the app's
    files anyway unless this file says otherwise. Without the file the behaviour
    is whatever the platform happens to default to, which is not the same thing
    as a decision.

    WHAT IS EXCLUDED, AND WHY ONLY THIS. filesDir/logs holds easy_voice.log and
    its three rotations, the diagnostic file the owner shares when reporting a
    bug, up to 2 MB each. It describes the phone it was written on, so carrying
    it to a new phone would move stale evidence and nothing else. Excluded from
    both paths.

    EVERYTHING ELSE IS DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE. The language list, the per
    language voice, speed, pitch and volume, the mode and the Advanced flags are
    exactly what a blind user would otherwise have to set up again by hand on a
    new phone, and the app reconciles them against a fresh engine scan on every
    open, so a configuration that arrives naming an engine this phone does not
    have is repaired rather than left broken. cacheDir is never backed up by the
    platform, so the exported settings copy under cache/shared needs no rule.

    (Note for anyone editing this file: an XML comment may not contain two
    consecutive hyphens, which is what tools/check/xmlcheck.py caught here.)
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="file" path="logs" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="file" path="logs" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
